---
import StudioLayout from '../../layouts/StudioLayout.astro';
import revisionScreens from '../../snippets/kin-revision.html?raw';
import '../../styles/kinematics.css';
---
<StudioLayout title="Kinematics - Physics with Harshith" chapterChip="Physics · Kinematics">

  <!-- =========== HOME =========== -->
  <section id="home" class="screen active">
    <div class="hero">
      <h1>Kine<span class="accent">matics</span></h1>
      <p>Watch motion happen, then take the controls - launch projectiles, read graphs, and race the river.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">

      <div class="tile" onclick="go('projectile')">
        <div class="tile-num">01</div>
        <div class="tile-icon ic-build"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 20c4-12 10-16 18-16"/><path d="M17 3l4 1-1 4"/><circle cx="5" cy="19" r="1.6" fill="#fff"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Projectile Playground</h3>
        <p>Set speed, angle and gravity - launch, watch the parabola, and read T, H and R live.</p>
        <span class="tile-go">Start ›</span>
      </div>

      <div class="tile" onclick="go('gravity')">
        <div class="tile-num">02</div>
        <div class="tile-icon ic-grid"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="4.6" r="2.2"/><path d="M12 9v7"/><path d="M8.5 12.8L12 16.3l3.5-3.5"/><path d="M4 21h16"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Motion Under Gravity</h3>
        <p>Drop it, throw it down, throw it up - one acceleration, one sign convention, every trap on screen.</p>
        <span class="tile-go">Start ›</span>
      </div>

      <div class="tile" onclick="go('graphs')">
        <div class="tile-num">03</div>
        <div class="tile-icon ic-sort"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M3 17l5-6 4 3 6-8"/><path d="M3 21h18"/></svg></div>
        <h3>Motion Graphs</h3>
        <p>Slope going down, area going up - read tangents, watch areas fill, and climb the shape ladder.</p>
        <span class="tile-go">Start ›</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========== PROJECTILE PLAYGROUND =========== -->
  <section id="projectile" class="screen">
    <div class="scr-head">
      <button class="back-btn" onclick="go('home')">‹ Back</button>
      <div>
        <div class="scr-title">Projectile Playground</div>
        <div class="scr-sub">Horizontal: constant velocity · Vertical: free fall · The only link is time.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kin-controls">
      <div class="kin-ctrl">
        <label>Speed u <span class="kin-val" id="uVal">25 m/s</span></label>
        <input type="range" id="uSlider" min="5" max="50" step="1" value="25">
      </div>
      <div class="kin-ctrl">
        <label>Angle θ <span class="kin-val" id="thetaVal">45°</span></label>
        <input type="range" id="thetaSlider" min="10" max="80" step="1" value="45">
      </div>
      <div class="kin-ctrl">
        <label>Gravity g <span class="kin-val" id="gVal">10 m/s²</span></label>
        <select id="gSelect">
          <option value="10" selected>Earth (g = 10)</option>
          <option value="9.8">Earth (g = 9.8)</option>
          <option value="1.62">Moon (g = 1.62)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-btns">
        <button class="check-btn" id="launchBtn">Launch 🚀</button>
        <button class="btn-reset" id="resetBtn">↺ Reset</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kin-canvas" id="projCanvas"></div>

    <div class="kin-stats">
      <div class="kin-stat">
        <div class="kin-stat-name">Time of flight</div>
        <div class="kin-formula" id="fT"></div>
        <div class="kin-stat-val" id="vT">-</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-stat">
        <div class="kin-stat-name">Maximum height</div>
        <div class="kin-formula" id="fH"></div>
        <div class="kin-stat-val" id="vH">-</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-stat">
        <div class="kin-stat-name">Horizontal range</div>
        <div class="kin-formula" id="fR"></div>
        <div class="kin-stat-val" id="vR">-</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========== PRACTICE - 50 QUESTIONS =========== -->
  <section id="practice50" class="screen">
    <div class="scr-head">
      <button class="back-btn" onclick="go('home')">‹ Back</button>
      <div>
        <div class="scr-title">Practice - 50 Questions</div>
        <div class="scr-sub">Lectures 1-4 · easy to medium · pick a section or run all fifty. Solve first, then reveal.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="score-pill"><div><div class="s-val" id="prCounter">1/50</div><div class="s-lab">Question</div></div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="rev-chips" id="prChips"></div>

    <div class="rev-card">
      <div class="rf-tag" id="prTag"></div>
      <div class="rf-text" id="prText"></div>
      <div class="rf-ans rev-step" id="prAns"></div>
      <div class="rev-ctrl-row" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <button class="check-btn" id="prReveal">Show answer</button>
        <button class="btn-reset" id="prPrev">‹ Previous</button>
        <button class="btn-reset" id="prNext">Next ›</button>
        <a class="btn-reset" href="/downloads/Kinematics_Practice_50Q.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:none;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;">⬇ Worksheet PDF</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rev-card">
      <div class="rev-q" style="font-size:16px;">Jump to a question</div>
      <div class="pr-grid" id="prGrid"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========== MOTION UNDER GRAVITY =========== -->
  <section id="gravity" class="screen">
    <div class="scr-head">
      <button class="back-btn" onclick="go('home')">‹ Back</button>
      <div>
        <div class="scr-title">Motion Under Gravity</div>
        <div class="scr-sub">UP is positive, so a = −g = −10 m/s², always. Get the signs right and every problem is the same problem.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rev-chips" id="gravTabs">
      <button class="rev-chip active" data-pane="gravSign">1 · Sign Ritual</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="gravDrop">2 · Drop It</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="gravUp">3 · Throw It Up</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="gravChase">4 · Two-Ball Chase</button>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 1 · Sign Ritual ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane active" id="gravSign">
      <div class="rev-keybox">
        <b>The ritual:</b> choose UP = positive once, then obey it for <b>every</b> quantity, for the <b>entire</b> problem.
        Up is +, down is −, and a = −10 m/s² no matter which way the ball moves.
        Most free-fall mistakes are convention violations, not algebra errors.
      </div>
      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag" id="gsTag">Sign ritual · Question 1 / 8</div>
        <div class="rev-q" id="gsQ"></div>
        <div class="rev-opts" id="gsOpts"></div>
        <div class="rev-feedback" id="gsFb"></div>
        <div class="rev-nav">
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gsPrev">‹ Previous</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gsNext">Next ›</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 2 · Drop It ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="gravDrop">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Tower height h <span class="kin-val" id="gdHVal">45 m</span></label>
          <input type="range" id="gdH" min="20" max="80" step="5" value="45">
        </div>
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Throw-down speed <span class="kin-val" id="gdUVal">0 m/s (dropped)</span></label>
          <input type="range" id="gdU" min="0" max="15" step="1" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="gdGo">Release</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gdPause">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gdReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="gdCanvas"></div>
      <div class="kin-stats">
        <div class="kin-stat">
          <div class="kin-stat-name">Time to land</div>
          <div class="kin-formula" id="gdFT"></div>
          <div class="kin-stat-val" id="gdVT">-</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-stat">
          <div class="kin-stat-name">Impact speed</div>
          <div class="kin-formula" id="gdFV"></div>
          <div class="kin-stat-val" id="gdVV">-</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        Watch the amber slices: a <b>dropped</b> ball covers 5 m, then 15 m, then 25 m in successive seconds -
        the <b>1 : 3 : 5 odd-number pattern</b>. Nudge the throw-down speed and see the pattern shift.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 3 · Throw It Up ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="gravUp">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Launch speed u <span class="kin-val" id="guUVal">20 m/s</span></label>
          <input type="range" id="guU" min="10" max="30" step="1" value="20">
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="guGo">Throw</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="guPause">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="guReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="guCanvas"></div>
      <div class="kin-stats">
        <div class="kin-stat">
          <div class="kin-stat-name">Time to top</div>
          <div class="kin-formula" id="guFT"></div>
          <div class="kin-stat-val" id="guVT">-</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-stat">
          <div class="kin-stat-name">Maximum height</div>
          <div class="kin-formula" id="guFH"></div>
          <div class="kin-stat-val" id="guVH">-</div>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-stat">
          <div class="kin-stat-name">Total flight time</div>
          <div class="kin-formula" id="guFTT"></div>
          <div class="kin-stat-val" id="guVTT">-</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        The flight <b>freezes at the top</b> so you can see it: v = 0, but a = −g, still.
        And symmetry only works when start and end heights are the <b>same</b> - a cliff or a rooftop breaks it.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 4 · Two-Ball Chase ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="gravChase">
      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rev-q">Ball A is dropped. One second later, ball B is dropped from the same point. As they fall, the gap between them...</div>
        <div class="rev-opts" id="gcOpts">
          <button class="rev-opt" data-ans="const">Stays constant</button>
          <button class="rev-opt" data-ans="grow">Keeps growing</button>
          <button class="rev-opt" data-ans="shrink">Shrinks</button>
        </div>
        <div class="rev-feedback" id="gcFb">
          Both have the same acceleration g - but A has been falling longer, so A is <b>always faster</b> than B.
          A keeps pulling away, so the gap keeps growing. Now run it and watch.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Release gap <span class="kin-val" id="gcGapVal">1 s</span></label>
          <input type="range" id="gcGap" min="0.5" max="2" step="0.5" value="1">
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="gcGo">Drop Both</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gcPause">⏸ Pause</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="gcReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="gcCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;" id="gcLog">
        <b>The two-body method:</b> one common origin, one common clock t, write each ball's position on that clock, then subtract.
        The same recipe solves lifts, windows and every meeting problem.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- =========== MOTION GRAPHS =========== -->
  <section id="graphs" class="screen">
    <div class="scr-head">
      <button class="back-btn" onclick="go('home')">‹ Back</button>
      <div>
        <div class="scr-title">Motion Graphs</div>
        <div class="scr-sub">Two keys unlock every graph: SLOPE going down the chain (x → v → a), AREA going up (a → v → x).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rev-chips" id="mgTabs">
      <button class="rev-chip active" data-pane="mgSlope">1 · Slope Reader</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgPath">2 · Not the Path!</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgArea">3 · Area Builder</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgLadder">4 · Shape Ladder</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgQuiz">5 · Rapid Fire</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgWorked">6 · Worked Examples</button>
      <button class="rev-chip" data-pane="mgHwk">7 · Homework</button>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 1 · Slope Reader ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane active" id="mgSlope">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl" style="flex:2;">
          <label>Drag along the curve <span class="kin-val">tangent follows you</span></label>
          <input type="range" id="mgsT" min="0" max="10" step="0.05" value="0">
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="mgsPlay">▶ Play</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgsReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="mgsCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <b>The first key:</b> slope of x-t = velocity. Steep = fast, flat = at rest, downhill = moving backward.
        And watch the rest segment: it is the <b>highest</b> part of the graph, yet the speed there is <b>zero</b> - height is not speed.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 2 · Not the Path ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgPath">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Motion of the car <span class="kin-val">same road every time</span></label>
          <select id="mgpMode">
            <option value="accel" selected>Speeding up on a flat road</option>
            <option value="uniform">Uniform velocity</option>
            <option value="return">Out and back</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="mgpPlay">▶ Play</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgpReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="mgpCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        The road is flat and straight - but the graph <b>curves</b>. An x-t graph is <b>never a picture of the path</b>:
        it plots the position coordinate against time. A rising graph does not mean the object goes "up".
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 3 · Area Builder ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgArea">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>v-t graph <span class="kin-val">area fills as time runs</span></label>
          <select id="mgaPreset">
            <option value="ramp" selected>Ramp up, then cruise (0→20 in 4 s, flat 6 s)</option>
            <option value="tri">Triangle (0→30 in 3 s, back to 0 at 9 s)</option>
            <option value="rev">Forward then reverse (+5 for 4 s, −5 for 2 s)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="mgaPlay">▶ Play</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgaReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="mgaCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        <b>The second key:</b> area under v-t = displacement, and the area <b>carries a sign</b>.
        Green area above the axis counts positive, red area below counts negative -
        so displacement subtracts while distance adds. Distance vs displacement from day one, drawn as regions.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 4 · Shape Ladder ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgLadder">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl">
          <label>Motion type <span class="kin-val">all three graphs, one motion</span></label>
          <select id="mglMode">
            <option value="rest">At rest</option>
            <option value="uniform">Uniform velocity</option>
            <option value="accel" selected>Uniform acceleration (from rest)</option>
            <option value="slow">Slowing down</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="check-btn" id="mglPlay">▶ Play</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mglReset">↺ Reset</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="mglCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-keybox" style="margin-top:16px;">
        The shape ladder: slope (differentiate) <b>lowers</b> the degree - parabola → line → flat.
        Area (integrate) <b>raises</b> it - flat → line → parabola.
        Once this is automatic, you can sketch any graph from any other with zero numbers.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 5 · Rapid Fire quiz ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgQuiz">
      <div class="rev-keybox">
        Ten quick readings, zero algebra. Every one of these is a guaranteed-marks exam question.
      </div>
      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag" id="mgqTag">Graph rapid fire · Question 1 / 10</div>
        <div class="rev-q" id="mgqQ"></div>
        <div class="rev-opts" id="mgqOpts"></div>
        <div class="rev-feedback" id="mgqFb"></div>
        <div class="rev-nav">
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgqPrev">‹ Previous</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgqNext">Next ›</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 6 · Worked Examples ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgWorked">
      <div class="kin-controls">
        <div class="kin-ctrl" style="flex:2;">
          <label>Worked example <span class="kin-val">step through the solution</span></label>
          <select id="mgwPick">
            <option value="slope" selected>L6 · Read acceleration from a v-t graph</option>
            <option value="tri">L7 · Displacement from a v-t triangle</option>
            <option value="sign">L7 · Sign of area: distance vs displacement</option>
            <option value="ramp">L7 · Mixed problem: ramp then cruise</option>
            <option value="conv">L7 · Convert a v-t line into a and x</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="kin-btns">
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgwPrev">‹ Back</button>
          <button class="check-btn" id="mgwNext">Next step ›</button>
          <button class="btn-reset" id="mgwReset">↺ Restart</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="kin-canvas" id="mgwCanvas"></div>
      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag" id="mgwTag"></div>
        <div class="rf-text" id="mgwProblem"></div>
        <div id="mgwSteps" style="margin-top:8px;"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Pane 7 · Homework ── -->
    <div class="grav-pane" id="mgHwk">
      <div class="rev-keybox">
        Homework for both graph lectures. <b>Sketch first, then reveal</b> - graphs reward the student
        who draws before they compute. Slope going down the chain, area going up.
      </div>

      <h3 class="hw-head">Lecture 6 · Reading slopes</h3>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 6 · Q1 · Sketch</div>
        <div class="rf-text">Sketch the x-t and v-t graphs for a ball thrown straight up and caught at the same height. Mark the highest point on each.</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          <b>x-t:</b> a downward parabola - position rises, curves over at the top, then falls back to the start height.
          The <b>highest point of the parabola</b> is the peak of the throw.<br>
          <b>v-t:</b> a straight line of slope −g, starting at +u, passing through zero, ending at −u.
          The highest point of the flight is where this line <b>crosses the time axis (v = 0)</b> - not the top of any curve.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 6 · Q2</div>
        <div class="rf-text">An x-t graph is a straight line from (0, 2 m) to (4 s, 10 m). Find the velocity. Is the motion uniform?</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          v = slope = (10 − 2) / (4 − 0) = <b>2 m/s</b>.
          The graph is a straight line, so the slope is constant everywhere: <b>yes, uniform velocity</b>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 6 · Q3</div>
        <div class="rf-text">A v-t graph rises 0 → 30 m/s in 3 s, then falls 30 → 0 m/s in 6 s. Find the acceleration in each phase (slope only).</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Phase 1: a = slope = (30 − 0) / 3 = <b>+10 m/s²</b>.<br>
          Phase 2: a = slope = (0 − 30) / 6 = <b>−5 m/s²</b> (still moving forward, but slowing down).
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 6 · Q4 · Conceptual</div>
        <div class="rf-text">What motion gives a horizontal x-t line? A straight slanted x-t line? A parabolic x-t curve?</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Horizontal x-t → position not changing → <b>at rest</b>.<br>
          Straight slanted x-t → equal metres in equal seconds → <b>uniform velocity</b>.<br>
          Parabolic x-t → slope changing steadily → <b>uniform acceleration</b>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <h3 class="hw-head">Lecture 7 · The area method</h3>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 7 · Q1</div>
        <div class="rf-text">A v-t graph: 0 → 30 m/s over 3 s, then 30 → 0 m/s over 6 s. Find total displacement, total distance, and the acceleration in each phase.</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Displacement = area = ½ · (base 9 s) · (height 30) = <b>135 m</b>.
          The graph never dips below the axis, so <b>distance = 135 m</b> too.<br>
          Acceleration: phase 1 = 30/3 = <b>+10 m/s²</b>; phase 2 = −30/6 = <b>−5 m/s²</b>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 7 · Q2</div>
        <div class="rf-text">A v-t graph spends 4 s at +6 m/s, then 3 s at −4 m/s. Find the displacement and the distance.</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Area above = 6 · 4 = +24 m. Area below = 4 · 3 = −12 m.<br>
          Displacement = 24 − 12 = <b>12 m</b> (signs subtract).
          Distance = 24 + 12 = <b>36 m</b> (magnitudes add).
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 7 · Q3</div>
        <div class="rf-text">An a-t graph is constant at 3 m/s² for 4 s (body starts from rest). Find the change in velocity and the displacement.</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Δv = area under a-t = 3 · 4 = <b>12 m/s</b>. From rest, final velocity = 12 m/s.<br>
          That builds a v-t line 0 → 12 m/s over 4 s, whose area is the displacement:
          ½ · 4 · 12 = <b>24 m</b>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rev-card">
        <div class="rf-tag">Lecture 7 · Q4 · Conceptual</div>
        <div class="rf-text">On a curved x-t graph, how do you find the instant of maximum speed? Why is "highest point" the wrong answer?</div>
        <button class="check-btn hw-reveal">Show solution</button>
        <div class="rf-ans rev-step">
          Maximum speed is where the x-t curve is <b>steepest</b> - largest magnitude of slope.
          "Highest point" is the largest <b>value of x</b>, which measures how far the object is, not how fast.
          At a smooth highest point the slope is actually <b>zero</b> (momentarily at rest), the opposite of fast.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

